1. **A multilayer display system, comprising:**

a power source;

a color-generating layer comprising a plurality of pixels, each pixel including a red sub-pixel, a green sub-pixel, and a blue sub-pixel;

a shutter layer disposed in optical alignment with the color-generating layer and comprising, for each pixel, a plurality of individually controllable shutter sub-pixels respectively corresponding to the red sub-pixel, the green sub-pixel, and the blue sub-pixel; and

an electronic controller electrically coupled to the power source, the color-generating layer, and the shutter layer, the electronic controller being configured to independently control the shutter sub-pixels between at least a light-transmissive state and a light-blocking state and to produce an opaque black pixel by placing each shutter sub-pixel corresponding to the red, green, and blue sub-pixels of the pixel in the light-blocking state.

A display system comprising:

a multilayer device having a rear side and an opposing viewing side;

a light source disposed adjacent the rear side and configured to direct light toward the viewing side;

a color layer positioned within the multilayer device and configured to spectrally modify light passing therethrough; and

a selectively controllable shutter layer positioned in an optical path extending from the rear side to the viewing side, the shutter layer comprising a plurality of shutter regions individually operable between at least a light-transmissive state and a light-attenuating state,

wherein light emitted by the light source propagates from the rear side toward the viewing side through the color layer and the selectively controllable shutter layer, and wherein selective operation of the shutter regions controls the spatial distribution of colored light presented at the viewing side.
